  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31404500",
      "title": "Using Response Data from POST Requests",
      "lectureOrder": 166,
      "videoOrder": 162,
      "sourceHash": "7e040701eef6844404f50eee34a4c1916ec70edd5669b6cba2c3c0b959854e20",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.45,
          "end": 4.43,
          "en": "Now, one thing I wanna improve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.43,
          "end": 8.93,
          "en": "about this app is the way I do fetch my expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.93,
          "end": 11.38,
          "en": "For example, I added a new expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.38,
          "end": 13.32,
          "en": "and it's added at the top here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.32,
          "end": 14.92,
          "en": "That's how we built our app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.92,
          "end": 18.52,
          "en": "That is the logic we set up in our expenses context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.52,
          "end": 20.44,
          "en": "When we add a new expense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.44,
          "end": 22.49,
          "en": "we add it at the beginning of this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.4,
          "end": 26.24,
          "en": "However, if I force a reload here and I switch back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.24,
          "end": 29.8,
          "en": "you see that latest expense is now at the bottom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.8,
          "end": 32.35,
          "en": "The reason for that is that on Firebase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.35,
          "end": 34.64,
          "en": "they are stored in chronological order.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.64,
          "end": 37.75,
          "en": "So, the newer expenses come at the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.75,
          "end": 40.5,
          "en": "and we have the older expenses at the beginning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.5,
          "end": 43.2,
          "en": "So, here it's not the date that matters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.2,
          "end": 46.14,
          "en": "but simply the time at which we added the expense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.14,
          "end": 48.59,
          "en": "no matter which date we set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.59,
          "end": 52.23,
          "en": "So it's the opposite logic of what we had before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.23,
          "end": 53.93,
          "en": "Now, I would like to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.93,
          "end": 57.04,
          "en": "that we keep the order we set up before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.04,
          "end": 60.1,
          "en": "and we could do this in this set reducer case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.1,
          "end": 64.72,
          "en": "where we do set our expenses to the fetched expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.72,
          "end": 67.71,
          "en": "Instead of just taking the fetched expenses like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.71,
          "end": 70.893,
          "en": "we could transform them and we could change the order.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.91,
          "end": 75.78999999999999,
          "en": "Now changing the order is rather straightforward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.78999999999999,
          "end": 79.49,
          "en": "We can get our inverted array by taking the original array;",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.49,
          "end": 81.42,
          "en": "which will be in our action payload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.42,
          "end": 84.7,
          "en": "and calling the reverse method on it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.7,
          "end": 86.23,
          "en": "which is built into JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.23,
          "end": 88.88,
          "en": "and which can be executed on arrays.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.88,
          "end": 92.72999999999999,
          "en": "And then it's this inverted array here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.72999999999999,
          "end": 94.9,
          "en": "With that, if we save that and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.9,
          "end": 98.08,
          "en": "our data is fetched again but now it has the same order",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.08,
          "end": 102.003,
          "en": "as it had when we started to add our expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102.93,
          "end": 104.69,
          "en": "Now, another change I wanna make",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.69,
          "end": 106.66,
          "en": "is also here in this reducer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.66,
          "end": 109.07,
          "en": "and that is related to this ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.07,
          "end": 111.97,
          "en": "We did generate our own ID in the past",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.97,
          "end": 113.94,
          "en": "but please remember that I mentioned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 113.94,
          "end": 117.47999999999999,
          "en": "that Firebase builds real unique IDs for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.47999999999999,
          "end": 119.82,
          "en": "And of course we should use these IDs because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.82,
          "end": 124.82,
          "en": "we also will need them later when we delete or update items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.85,
          "end": 127.79,
          "en": "We need to be able to target the correct expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.79,
          "end": 129.163,
          "en": "on the backend then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.04,
          "end": 131.91,
          "en": "Now if we build our own IDs here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 131.91,
          "end": 134.78,
          "en": "when we add an expense, that will be a problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 134.78,
          "end": 137,
          "en": "because this code is still relevant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 137,
          "end": 139.24,
          "en": "because we do still add expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.24,
          "end": 141.22,
          "en": "to the context when we do add them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 141.22,
          "end": 144.38,
          "en": "And we do still use our context in the app;",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.38,
          "end": 148.18,
          "en": "for all the reasons explained in the previous lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 148.18,
          "end": 151.1,
          "en": "Therefore, instead of creating our own ID here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 151.1,
          "end": 152.82,
          "en": "we should get rid of that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 152.82,
          "end": 156.153,
          "en": "and use the ID returned by Firebase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 157.54,
          "end": 161.38,
          "en": "So, actually, I expect my action payload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 161.38,
          "end": 163.48,
          "en": "to be the full expense object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 163.48,
          "end": 166.95,
          "en": "that already contains a good ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 166.95,
          "end": 171.95,
          "en": "And with good ID, I mean the ID generated by Firebase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 172.3,
          "end": 175.73,
          "en": "That implies that we need to get hold of that ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.73,
          "end": 178.78,
          "en": "when we send a request to Firebase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 178.78,
          "end": 182.91,
          "en": "when we send an expense to Firebase to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 182.91,
          "end": 185.78,
          "en": "So here, when we post a new expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.78,
          "end": 189.963,
          "en": "we need to get the ID that was generated by Firebase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.9,
          "end": 194.46,
          "en": "Now, thankfully Firebase gives us that ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 194.46,
          "end": 197.36,
          "en": "in the response to this request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 197.36,
          "end": 199.57,
          "en": "So, therefore, we need to work with that response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 199.57,
          "end": 203.07,
          "en": "and hence I will again use async await here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 203.07,
          "end": 205.343,
          "en": "to get that response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 206.45,
          "end": 208.61,
          "en": "And then it's in this response data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 208.61,
          "end": 211.233,
          "en": "where we find the generated ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 212.12,
          "end": 215.19,
          "en": "Now the property in the data object that holds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 215.19,
          "end": 219.34,
          "en": "the auto generated ID is not called ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 219.34,
          "end": 222.3,
          "en": "Firebase didn't decide to use that name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 222.3,
          "end": 224.43,
          "en": "instead, there will be a name property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 224.43,
          "end": 227.44,
          "en": "that holds the auto-generated ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 227.44,
          "end": 230.28,
          "en": "You can find information like this in the official docs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 230.28,
          "end": 232.82999999999998,
          "en": "or simply take it from me here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 232.82999999999998,
          "end": 235.87,
          "en": "So that's the ID generated by Firebase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 235.87,
          "end": 238.82999999999998,
          "en": "We get it as part of the response when sending data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 238.82999999999998,
          "end": 243.14,
          "en": "to Firebase, we can then use is this ID, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 243.14,
          "end": 245.52,
          "en": "Because now we can return this ID here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 245.52,
          "end": 249.64,
          "en": "so that our store expense function returns a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 249.64,
          "end": 251.04,
          "en": "because it's async,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 251.04,
          "end": 254.133,
          "en": "which will then resolve to that ID in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 255.11,
          "end": 257.35,
          "en": "That means that in manage expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 257.35,
          "end": 261.78,
          "en": "where we do actually call this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 261.78,
          "end": 266.32,
          "en": "this store expense function; we will get back the ID here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 266.32,
          "end": 269.11,
          "en": "For this I will transform confirm handler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 269.11,
          "end": 270.7,
          "en": "into an async function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 270.7,
          "end": 273.2,
          "en": "so that we can await this here as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 273.2,
          "end": 275.75,
          "en": "because store expense will return a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 275.75,
          "end": 277.83,
          "en": "as I just said before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 277.83,
          "end": 279.84000000000003,
          "en": "And then, eventually we will get that ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 279.84000000000003,
          "end": 281.733,
          "en": "to which that promise resolves.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 282.6,
          "end": 285.09000000000003,
          "en": "And when we then call add expense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 285.09000000000003,
          "end": 287.71,
          "en": "we pass an object to add expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 287.71,
          "end": 291.57,
          "en": "that gets all the expense data we got from the input fields.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 291.57,
          "end": 294.88,
          "en": "But, where we also add an extra ID field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 294.88,
          "end": 297.823,
          "en": "which holds that ID we got back from the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 298.8,
          "end": 302.13,
          "en": "So this ID is now all the part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 302.13,
          "end": 306.213,
          "en": "of the object that we send to the context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 307.8,
          "end": 309.76,
          "en": "So that is now another important step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 309.76,
          "end": 311.603,
          "en": "for using the right ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 312.75,
          "end": 314.28,
          "en": "And with that, if we save this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 314.28,
          "end": 318.98,
          "en": "we are still able to add something here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 318.98,
          "end": 322.07,
          "en": "and here I will now pick a different date",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 322.07,
          "end": 325,
          "en": "so that it shows up under all expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 325,
          "end": 328.43,
          "en": "And this will now have gotten the proper ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 328.43,
          "end": 330.873,
          "en": "The ID managed by Firebase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 332.01,
          "end": 334.96,
          "en": "So that's another important step forward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 334.96,
          "end": 337.48,
          "en": "As a next step, we can now make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 337.48,
          "end": 341.603,
          "en": "that we can also update and delete our data on Firebase.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
